assemblies. It does name them. I could include:\n- role: \"A/D conversion module\"\n- role: \"main board with processor\"\n\nMaybe also interfaces as components: RS232C serial port, Centronic printer port. Those are interfaces, could be components. I'll include them perhaps. Let me keep components minimal: ad_conversion_module, main_board_with_processor. And maybe interfaces listed under type_level characteristics or a separate section. I could add config_level? No.\n\ncharacteristics:\ntype_level (whole-cert attributes):\n- power_supply: multiple forms. Let me parse:\n  - \"9-12 VDC via mains adaptor (9V / 500 mA); 6 V / 4Ah rechargeable battery\"\n  \n  So:\n  - power_supply_voltage: {min: 9, max: 12}, unit \"V\" (DC)\n  - mains_adaptor_output: 9 V / 500 mA → voltage 9 V, current 500 mA\n  - battery: 6 V, 4 Ah rechargeable\n  - power_supply_type: DC (\"VDC\")\n  \n  I could emit:\n  - power_supply_voltage: value {min 9, max 12}, unit_symbol \"V\"\n  - mains_adaptor_voltage: 9 V\n  - mains_adaptor_current: 500 mA\n  - battery_voltage: 6 V\n  - battery_capacity: 4 Ah\n  - load_cell_excitation_voltage: 5 V (DC)\n  - load_cell_impedance: {min: 85, max: 1100}, unit \"Ω\"\n  - min_input_voltage_per_interval: 1, unit \"µV\"\n  - measuring_range: {min: -9.7, max: 19.5}, unit \"mV\"\n  - dead_load_signal_voltage: {min: 0, max: 10}, unit \"mV\"\n  - fraction_of_max_permissible_error: 0.5 — attribute p_ind = 0.5. Use \"indicator_fraction_of_max_permissible_error\" or \"fraction_of_max_permissible_error_p_ind\": 0.5.\n  - operating_temperature: {min: -10, max: 40}, unit \"°C\"\n  - max_load_cell_cable_length_6_wire: 30 m\n  - software_version: \"V1.2\" (string value)\n  \n  Class-dependent: \"Max scale intervals: 10,000 (Class III); 1,000 (Class IIII)\" — this is config-level varying by accuracy class. Use config_level:\n  - attribute: max_scale_intervals, axis: accuracy_class, values: [{condition: \"Class III\", value: 10000}, {condition: \"Class IIII\", value: 1000}]\n\n  M